      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T03:08:40Z"
      },
      "message": "Merge upstream/main into issue/3474-same-angle-arc\n\nResolve the conflict in crates/post/src/post/arc_guard.rs: keep main's\nexact stream endpoint equality for a full turn (532d0fa92) and this\nbranch's _arcSweep helper for the sweep.\n\nfix(post): read the same-angle rule about the centre the control computes\n\nA post that writes I J K as increments from the start now passes\ninc(axis, delta) to arcFate / arcFateOf. The rule adds the written\nincrement to the written start, so it uses the control's centre and not\nthe rounded absolute centre. The mill posts pass arcIncOf(fu); the\nlathes double the radius I to the diameter X scale. The Heidenhain posts\nwrite an absolute centre and pass no inc.\n\nPinned by a_same_angle_arc_about_the_written_incremental_centre_posts_as_its_straight_move\n(mm and inch) and the offset-* rows of\narc_fate_reads_a_same_angle_short_arc_as_a_straight_move.\n\nRefs #3474\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
